Full rebuild prompt: Israa Ellban portfolio
One prompt for the whole site, rebuilt from scratch. Part 0 is for you. The prompt starts at Part 1 and continues to the end of the document.
الجزء 0: ملاحظات ليكي
إزاي تستخدميه: الصقي الدوكيمنت كله من الجزء 1 لآخره في أداة الفايب كود في رسالة واحدة، وارفعي معاه الصور بنفس الأسماء المكتوبة في قسم 13. ارفعي كمان الـ 4 اسكرين شوتس اللي بعتيهملي كمراجع (اسمائهم في قسم 13).
قرارات أخدتها من كلامك، راجعيها:
• الاسم Israa Ellban زي ما هو في الاسكرين شوت. الاسم العربي الكامل مش عندي، فكتبت “إسراء” بس [CONFIRM].
• قسم الإبداع (الخط والهوايات) اتلغى من الصفحة ومن الناف بار.
• الناف بار: Journey · Experiences · Skills · Learning · Connect. دمجت الكورسات والتعليم في قسم Learning.
• مشهد الشبكة المتداخلة (CVeeeZ) انتقل جوه بوب اب الخبرة ومش مشهد مستقل.
• زرار “Let there be light” اللي في الاسكرين شوت شيلته. لو عايزاه قوليلي.
• حطيت سكشن صغير للمشاريع بعنوان “بتتحدّث” قبل Connect. شيليه لو مش عايزاه.
• كلمة مميزة في كل عنوان بتتلون بلون مختلف (لافندر أو وردي)، زي ما طلبتي.
محتاجة منك قبل اللصق:
• التعليم: اسم الجامعة والكلية والسنة (ميكروبيولوجي).
• الكورسات: اسم الجهة والسنة لكل كورس، واسم جهة كورس المهارات الشخصية (كتبتي “ماي كنسي”).
• قايمة الـ soft skills اللي خدتيها من الكورس.
• لوجوهات الشركات الأربعة (هتتحط جوه ميداليات الخبرات زي اللي موجود دلوقتي).
• الإيميل: كتبتي gamil وأنا كتبت gmail. التليفون هيظهر لأي حد، لو مش عايزة شيليه من قسم 12.
Part 1: the prompt starts here
1. Project, stack, tokens
Build the entire portfolio from scratch as a bilingual (English and Arabic, with a language toggle that mirrors layout, paths and reading direction to RTL) single-page scroll experience for Israa Ellban. It is a storybook world: a castle, a cat, stacks of books, leaves, a river, a stone bridge, a paper boat, a lantern. The uploaded reference screenshots (ref-navbar, ref-dark-gate, ref-hero-light, ref-journey-scratches) define the exact look of the navbar, the dark gate, the hero and the journey slide; match them closely.
Stack: use React, Vite, GSAP with ScrollTrigger, and Lenis. Tokens: hero cream #F5EFE0, cream #FBEEE1, peach #F5D9C3, lavender #A68BC8 and #E4D8F0, sage #9DB5A0, rose #EDA89B, coral #E7907A, amber #E3B26E, deep plum #2D2140, night #0B0814. Fonts: Playfair Display (headings, with italic for accent words) and Plus Jakarta Sans (body) for English; Noto Naskh Arabic (headings) and Readex Pro (body) for Arabic. Highlight rule: in every headline, one key word is set in an accent color (lavender or rose, often in Playfair italic) so each headline has a clear focal word. Night mode (moon button) swaps cream and peach surfaces for plum surfaces and keeps illustrations untouched; the dark gate is always dark.
Use only the uploaded illustrations, referenced by file name. Never draw geometric stand-in art and never use emoji. If an image is missing, render a dashed paper-textured rectangle labeled with the file name, and keep all animation working on it. UI parts (chips, counters, cards, notes, buttons) are drawn in code as soft paper components with rounded corners, paper grain and soft shadows.
2. Feel rules (apply to every animation)
• Curves only. Every path, trail or arc is a long smooth Bézier. No straight connectors, no angular zigzags, nothing snaps.
• Easing: default cubic-bezier(.45,0,.2,1); entrances cubic-bezier(.22,.8,.3,1); settling with a tiny overshoot cubic-bezier(.34,1.3,.5,1). Micro 250 to 350 ms, reveals 800 to 1100 ms, scenes 1.6 to 2.2 s, stagger 80 to 120 ms.
• Lines are drawn with stroke-dashoffset on round-capped paths with slightly uneven width, as if inked by pen. Idle motion is irregular, never metronomic.
• Text reveals: words rise 16 to 36 px with a blur-to-sharp fade. Vignettes and reveals have feathered edges.
• Pointer: foreground foliage shifts opposite the pointer up to 14 px, midground 6, background 3; illustrated objects tilt toward the pointer up to 6 degrees; on light scenes the pointer leaves two or three fading sparkles.
• Scroll-linked motion follows scroll with slight inertia. Respect prefers-reduced-motion by showing final states with gentle fades.
• Never: spinning, flashing, neon glow, bouncing cartoon physics, hard cuts.
3. Sound system
Synthesize all sounds with Web Audio (soft and warm), master volume about 0.35, unlocked by the first user gesture (the lantern pull), with a navbar toggle (“Sound On / Sound Off”) whose state is remembered. If an optional file exists (for example sfx-scratch.mp3) use it instead of the synthesized version. Events: lantern pull (soft click then a warm two-note chime); typewriter tick on each typed character (very soft, pitch varied about 4%); name landing in the navbar (soft pop); wave rising (airy whoosh); each journey beat (soft pluck); the scribble over “scratches” (a pen-on-paper scratch: band-passed noise around 1.8 to 3.5 kHz, three bursts of about 220 ms synced to the three strokes); station bloom (glass chime, pitch rising with station index); popup opening (paper rustle); skill piece bloom (marimba pluck rising); piece into pocket (soft whoosh and tick); each SKILL tile (soft click); SKILL complete (ascending arpeggio); burst (quiet shimmer); book on shelf (wooden thud); boat sailing (water); copy button (ping).
4. Navbar and global controls
Match ref-navbar. A translucent cream bar with a thin bottom hairline. Inline-start: a small lavender dot and the logo text “Israa Ellban” in Playfair Display semibold; this logo slot stays empty until the hero name lands in it (Scene 1). Center: Journey, Experiences, Skills, Learning, Connect (Plus Jakarta Sans, about 15 px); the active link gets a lavender underline drawn like a pen stroke with a slight curve; clicking scrolls with Lenis (1.4 s, soft easing). Inline-end: an EN | AR segmented pill, a Sound toggle pill with a speaker icon, and a circular moon button for Night mode. In Arabic the whole bar mirrors. The navbar is hidden during the dark gate and slides down softly when the light arrives. On mobile the links collapse into a menu button that opens a soft sheet.
5. Scene 0: the dark gate
Copy. EN: “It’s a bit dark in here.” / “Mind pulling that lantern?” / button “Pull lantern” / tooltip “Pull or tap the lantern cord”. AR: “المكان ضلمة شوية..” / “تسحبي الفانوس؟” / “اسحب الفانوس” / “اسحب أو اضغط على حبل الفانوس”.
Visual. The first thing the visitor sees is a nearly black page (night #0B0814). The only things visible are the centered text and a single lit lantern (gate-lantern) hanging from a thin drawn cord near the top inline-end corner, as in ref-dark-gate. The full night illustration (gate-night-scene: moon, bridge, river, paper boat, cat, castle) exists but is hidden in darkness.
Motion.
• The lantern sways slowly left and right like a pendulum on a long cord, about 6 degrees each way on a 5.5 s period with about 10% irregularity. Its warm halo flickers softly (opacity between 0.85 and 1, irregular) and a few tiny embers drift upward.
• The pointer is a lantern light: a feathered warm glow (radius about 200 px, #F4C95D at roughly 16%) follows the pointer with lerp 0.15, and through a radial mask it reveals gate-night-scene (up to about 85% opacity inside the light). The lantern reveals the area around itself in the same way, following its sway. Nothing else is lit.
• The tooltip near the lantern fades after the first interaction.
• Pull: the visitor drags the cord down up to 40 px with an elastic stretch (or presses the button, or Enter or Space on the focused cord), then releases; the lantern swings back with a damped swing, flares (halo three times larger for about 400 ms) and a warm bloom expands from the lantern as a feathered circle over about 1.8 s, dissolving the night and revealing Scene 1 beneath. Play the lantern-pull sound. Scroll is locked during the gate and until the hero intro completes (a small “Skip” link appears after 2 s).
