14. Layout, scroll and performance rules
• Target viewports: 1366x650, 1280x600, 1920x950, 390x844, and browser zoom 67% to 150%. Everything a scene shows must be visible inside one viewport at those sizes. Use svh and dvh, never vh.
• Every pinned scene is an outer section of height N x 100svh containing a sticky stage (top 0, height 100svh, overflow hidden) with a fixed design canvas (1440x800) scaled by min(100vw/1440, 100svh/800), centered. Titles, captions, cards, pieces and panels live inside this canvas; nothing sits below the fold.
• One ScrollTrigger per scene (start top top, end bottom bottom, scrub 1) drives a single GSAP timeline of total duration 1 with labeled beats; text, pieces and counters all derive from that progress so the pocket counter, the pieces and the SKILL assembly always match. No independent reveal triggers firing elsewhere.
• Base CSS shows every text and image in its final state; animate with gsap.fromTo only; never ship opacity 0 in base CSS; with no JS or with reduced motion, final states show.
• Initialize Lenis once with lenis.on(“scroll”, ScrollTrigger.update), gsap.ticker.add((t) => lenis.raf(t * 1000)) and gsap.ticker.lagSmoothing(0). Remove CSS scroll-behavior smooth and scroll-snap. Anchor links use lenis.scrollTo.
• Animate only transform and opacity; no scroll-driven blur or box-shadow animation on large layers; will-change only during animation; contain layout paint on stages; no backdrop-filter on large layers; lazy-load and decode images before first use.
• Add a debug overlay (visible with ?debug=1) showing viewport size, active scene, scene progress 0 to 1 and active beat.
